WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.658
It's called The Shoe That Grows.

2
00:00:03.659 --> 00:00:09.361
What does it do? Well, it grows!

3
00:00:09.362 --> 00:00:14.733
This lets kids have shoes they can wear for a long time!

4
00:00:14.734 --> 00:00:22.129
In 2007 Kenton Lee was working at an orphanage in Kenya.

5
00:00:22.130 --> 00:00:26.378
One day he was walking with a group of kids.

6
00:00:26.379 --> 00:00:28.876
He looked down at a little girl.

7
00:00:28.877 --> 00:00:33.047
She had on a white dress and shoes that didn't fit.

8
00:00:33.048 --> 00:00:39.574
The front parts of the shoes were cut open, and the girl's toes were sticking out.

9
00:00:39.575 --> 00:00:42.412
Kenton looked around.

10
00:00:42.413 --> 00:00:49.595
Many other kids' shoes were much too small for their feet.

11
00:00:49.596 --> 00:00:56.104
Kenton asked the orphanage director why so many kids had shoes that didn't fit.

12
00:00:56.105 --> 00:01:04.631
The director explained that the children outgrew their shoes quickly.

13
00:01:04.632 --> 00:01:09.270
And there simply weren't enough donated shoes for everyone.

14
00:01:09.271 --> 00:01:14.204
Kenton couldn't stop thinking about the children's shoes.

15
00:01:14.205 --> 00:01:20.295
Wearing small shoes was unhealthy for the children since their feet were still growing.

16
00:01:20.296 --> 00:01:23.329
But going barefoot was dangerous too.

17
00:01:23.330 --> 00:01:28.150
The children could get diseases from walking barefoot.

18
00:01:28.151 --> 00:01:31.500
Their feet could even become infected.

19
00:01:31.501 --> 00:01:36.419
There had to be a solution to this problem.

20
00:01:36.420 --> 00:01:39.440
Finally Kenton had an idea.

21
00:01:39.441 --> 00:01:42.494
He could create special shoes.

22
00:01:42.495 --> 00:01:45.889
His shoes would grow along with a child.

23
00:01:45.890 --> 00:01:51.484
The shoes couldn't be expensive, and they needed to last for a long time.

24
00:01:51.485 --> 00:01:57.071
Now Kenton just needed to find a way to make these shoes.

25
00:01:57.072 --> 00:02:04.403
He contacted several shoe companies, but none showed interest in his idea.

26
00:02:04.404 --> 00:02:08.059
Kenton decided to make the shoes himself.

27
00:02:08.060 --> 00:02:11.753
He even made himself a promise to show his commitment.

28
00:02:11.754 --> 00:02:17.284
He wouldn't buy himself a new pair of shoes until his project was finished.

29
00:02:17.285 --> 00:02:22.889
Five years later Kenton's shoes had holes and were worn out.

30
00:02:22.890 --> 00:02:29.232
But he had created a great new shoe—The Shoe That Grows!

31
00:02:29.233 --> 00:02:32.305
The shoes look like normal sandals.

32
00:02:32.306 --> 00:02:37.900
They're designed to last for five years, so all of their materials are durable.

33
00:02:37.901 --> 00:02:43.849
The straps can be adjusted with snaps, buckles, and Velcro.

34
00:02:43.850 --> 00:02:47.320
This lets the shoes grow along with the wearer.

35
00:02:47.321 --> 00:02:51.775
The shoes come in three sizes.

36
00:02:51.776 --> 00:02:55.824
Each can fit five different shoe sizes.

37
00:02:55.825 --> 00:02:59.659
Kenton designed the shoes to be small and light too.

38
00:02:59.660 --> 00:03:05.212
He wanted to send lots of shoes at once to poor places around the world.

39
00:03:05.213 --> 00:03:12.951
In fact, fifty pairs of these shoes can fit into a normal-sized duffel bag.

40
00:03:12.952 --> 00:03:17.216
Kenton's organization is called Because International.

41
00:03:17.217 --> 00:03:20.538
It relies on volunteers to deliver the shoes.

42
00:03:20.539 --> 00:03:24.855
Because International has also sent shoes to adults.

43
00:03:24.856 --> 00:03:28.629
Some of the shoes are even made in poor countries.

44
00:03:28.630 --> 00:03:33.410
So the shoes have created jobs for people too.

45
00:03:33.411 --> 00:03:40.649
With The Shoe That Grows, Kenton found a simple way to solve a serious problem.

46
00:03:40.650 --> 00:03:48.741
His shoe design has improved the lives of poor children around the world.

